@meta
id: 19-18
title: The list you had before
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: quickfix-nav, cdo
par: 185
minutes: 9
vscode: retype the first search and scroll back to where you were
vimrc: set hidden smartcase
open: README.md

@brief
Every `:vimgrep`, `:grep`, `:cfile` and `:make` replaces the quickfix
list. Vim keeps the last ten. `:colder` steps back to the previous
list, `:cnewer` forward again, and each list remembers which entry you
were on.

The job that gets interrupted: three calls on `this.paymentProducer`
under `src`, and two of them are missing their `await`, so a failed
publish is silently dropped. Each hit needs reading, because one
already has it, so this is a walk, not a `:cdo`.

Fix the first hit, then stop: the rename that has to land in the same
commit is `PaymentProducer.refundIssued` to `refundCompleted`, in the
producer, both providers and the test. Do it now, with `:vimgrep` and
`:cdo`, before you forget. That replaces the list you were walking.
Get it back with `:colder`, carry on from where you were, and add the
other missing `await`. `RefundIssuedEvent` is a type and keeps its
name.

@keys
| `:colder` | go back to the previous quickfix list |
| `:cnewer` | forward again |
| `:chistory` | show all the lists vim is holding |

@hints
`:vimgrep /this\.paymentProducer\./ **/*.ts`. Starting the pattern at
`this` puts the cursor where the `await` goes. The first hit is in the
order provider and has none: `i`, `await `, `Esc`, `:w`.
--
Now the rename: `:vimgrep /refundIssued/ **/*.ts` and
`:cdo s/refundIssued/refundCompleted/g | update`. Then `:colder`. The
message line says which list you are on.
--
`:cn`, read: the payment provider's first call already has its
`await`. `:cn` again: the second does not. Add it, `:wq`.

@solution
    :vimgrep /this\.paymentProducer\./ **/*.ts<Enter>  i await <Esc> :w<Enter>
    :vimgrep /refundIssued/ **/*.ts<Enter>  :cdo s/refundIssued/refundCompleted/g | update<Enter>
    :colder<Enter>  :cn<Enter> :cn<Enter>  i await <Esc> :wq<Enter>

`:colder` brought back a list whose first entry now points at a line
that reads differently from when it was found: the rename went through
it. The entry still pointed at the right place and the position was
still entry one, because vim keeps every list live, not as a snapshot.
The lists are a stack of up to ten; `:chistory` shows them with the
command that made each and the one you are on marked.

Lesson 13 solved the same interruption with a location list, by
deciding in advance that the walk would live somewhere the rename could
not touch. `:colder` is for when you did not decide in advance, which
is most of the time. Both are cheap; use whichever you remember first.

The other reason to reach for `:colder` is a search you narrowed too
far. `:vimgrep` broad, `:vimgrep` narrow, and the narrow one dropped
something you wanted: one `:colder` and the broad list is back without
retyping anything.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../payment/payment.producer';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);
    this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: order.id, receipt: 'pending' });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../payment/payment.producer';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);
    await this.paymentProducer.refundCompleted({ paymentId: order.id, receipt: 'pending' });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../payment/payment.producer';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const paymentProducer = stub<PaymentProducer>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService, paymentProducer);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).sendRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
    expect(paymentProducer.refundIssued).toHaveBeenCalled();
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
